From 27720df1918ad0d7e48f7fa1ab360bc2cf6be93d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:41:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] feat(kanban-sync): bounded opt-in sync timing
 diagnostics

Off unless the installation-root key kanban.sync.diagnostics.timing_until holds a
finite Unix time at most 600 s ahead. One capture per value, bounded by that time,
600 s monotonic, config change/read failure, write failure or the 32 MiB file cap.

- hermes_cli/kanban_sync_timing.py: allowlisted numeric/enum JSONL records to
  <root>/logs/kanban-sync-timing.jsonl (board ordinals, run nonce, pid, seq, boot
  code identity). Decoded feed change -> claimed at select under the same lock ->
  matched to that board's own service; failures return to pending with a count.
  Reporter outer span plus collect/limit/cpu/adv/send (whole private transport).
  Flush only at the loop's pre-wait boundary, its cost recorded separately.
  Lost/invalid/diagnostic-error/write-failure/file-cap captures are marked invalid.
- hermes_cli/kanban_sync_timing_report.py: neutral analyzer (validity, latency,
  overlap/non-overlap cohorts, overlap residual, failures, censored pending,
  report components, overhead). No thresholds, no baseline subtraction.
- Facade calls in kanban_sync_client (FeedWatcher, select, sync_all_once per board,
  report_due, wait, loop exit) and machine_metrics Reporter spans.

Proof: RED (import + 6 hook tests), GREEN unit + 2 real-loop tests, 86-file area
suite 1039 passed, scripts/check ok, 44 exact-anchor mutants all killed.
Tests validate instrumentation only; no live acceptance claimed.
